From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:37:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: s6sy761 - add touch_count sysfs attribute

Count completed touches (finger-up events) and expose the counter in
sysfs, as edt-ft5x06 does for the comma four. AGNOS reads it early in
boot to detect the tap pattern that requests a factory reset, which
includes taps made before any userspace input listener is running.

Unlike edt-ft5x06, this controller only scans once it gets SENSE_ON,
which the driver sends from the input device's open(). Send it at the
end of probe too, so the counter sees taps before anything opens the
device. On the comma 3X the UI keeps the device open whenever it runs,
so this doesn't change how long the controller scans in practice.

This is a local ABI and is not intended for upstream.

[adeeb: use DEVICE_ATTR_RO() and sysfs_emit() like the edt-ft5x06 one;
 send SENSE_ON at probe]
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c
index 899c179fb2..5d2f4b6b9c 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c
@@ -108,6 +108,8 @@ struct s6sy761_data {
 
 	u16 devid;
 	u8 tx_channel;
+
+	u64 touch_count;
 };
 
 /*
@@ -165,6 +167,7 @@ static void s6sy761_report_release(struct s6sy761_data *sdata,
 {
 	input_mt_slot(sdata->input, tid);
 	input_mt_report_slot_state(sdata->input, MT_TOOL_FINGER, false);
+	sdata->touch_count++;
 
 	input_sync(sdata->input);
 }
@@ -282,8 +285,19 @@ static ssize_t s6sy761_sysfs_devid(struct device *dev,
 
 static DEVICE_ATTR(devid, 0444, s6sy761_sysfs_devid, NULL);
 
+static ssize_t touch_count_show(struct device *dev,
+				struct device_attribute *attr, char *buf)
+{
+	struct s6sy761_data *sdata = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%llu\n", sdata->touch_count);
+}
+
+static DEVICE_ATTR_RO(touch_count);
+
 static struct attribute *s6sy761_sysfs_attrs[] = {
 	&dev_attr_devid.attr,
+	&dev_attr_touch_count.attr,
 	NULL
 };
 ATTRIBUTE_GROUPS(s6sy761_sysfs);
@@ -462,6 +476,11 @@ static int s6sy761_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
+	/* touch_count must see taps before any listener opens the device */
+	err = i2c_smbus_write_byte(sdata->client, S6SY761_SENSE_ON);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
+
 	pm_runtime_enable(&client->dev);
 
 	return 0;
